vapoursynth-colormatch
======================

This project is a reimplementation of a published method, not a port of code.

Method credit
-------------
The rotated-marginal colour matching approach implemented here originates in
"ColorMatch" (2015) by Menno Dreischor (DrDre), a MATLAB GUI tool for colour
matching between images, discussed in:

    Dr. Dre's Magical Color Matching Tool
    https://originaltrilogy.com/topic/Color-matching-and-prediction-color-correction-tool-v13-released/id/18128/

The MATLAB sources are archived at https://github.com/Miralia/dr-dre-colormatch
and are not used, copied, or linked into this project. What is reused is the
algorithm, which is not copyrightable subject matter:

  * building a transform by matching per-axis marginals in a set of rotated
    colour spaces, and accumulating the corrections in RGB;
  * the observation that the first direction should use the [0, 1] range while
    rotated directions use [-sqrt(3), +sqrt(3)].

Everything else differs, deliberately and substantially. See the "What it does
differently" table in README.md: pooled multi-frame sampling, linear-splatted
CDFs instead of quantile knots with a smoothing spline, uniform-grid tables
instead of binary search over knots, probability-band trimming, native float
evaluation instead of a baked 33^3 LUT, and an independent (unpaired) reference
side.

API conventions
---------------
The Python wrapper's argument naming and validation style follow the conventions
established by the surrounding VapourSynth ecosystem, in particular:

  * vs-jetpack (MIT) -- the `.vsjet` package storage layout, `PackageStorage`,
    and the `Backend.autoselect` shape;
  * vs_colorfix (Apache-2.0, pifroggi) -- inline `TypeError`/`ValueError`
    validation with the function name in the message, and the
    `backend=` / `gpu_id=` / `cache folder` argument vocabulary.

No code was copied from either project. These are naming and layout
conventions, adopted so that the tool feels native to the ecosystem.
